{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/360/spec.md 2>/dev/null || find attest/specs/360 -maxdepth 2 -type f -print; sed -n '1,180p' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp3644wusr/check-02.log; sed -n '1,180p' attest/records/360/build-02.log; rg -n \\\"mypy|ledger.py|permission|blocked|intervention|StatementIntervention|Edit tool|halt|question\\\" attest/records/360/build-02.log; rg -n \\\"item_acts_and_interventions|StatementIntervention|class Intervention|Intervention\\\" attavo schema tests /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp3644wusr/diff.patch\"","aggregated_output":"## Problem\n\nClass: fix\n\nThe reviews of the 2026-10-14 wave passed with four findings, none blocking, each a few lines. They are one item because each is small and they share a wave.\n\n1. #339's rejection test proves the claim's `at` equals the version's `at`, not that the clock is read once. A call count on `now_iso` for one `plan claims` write proves the stronger claim (the product already reads once; the test is what is missing).\n2. `store.put`'s own stamp, when the caller passes no `at`, has no regression test.\n3. #351's review read the gate as judging criterion kinds before the exit-code contract. The spec's own push found the contract is already judged first: a structural criterion that exits 1 on the tree and 2 on the stub is refused \"criterion could not check (exit 2)\" on main today. The finding needs no logic; its test pins the order.\n4. `attavo/types.py` types an intervention's `class` as `str`; the schema is the enum `amend`, `launch`, `transport`. A TypedDict for an intervention carries it as a `Literal`, and the mirror test reads enums against literals.\n\nThe stub is thin: the four tests, one per finding, in their files; the one that needs logic (4) is red on the stub. The build writes the logic.\n\nRetires: four gaps a second reader found that the first reader's tests did not cover.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/spec.py\n- attavo/types.py\n- tests/test_plan.py\n- tests/test_store.py\n- tests/test_spec_gate.py\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- [structural] the-rejection-tests-exist.sh: the four tests exist, one per finding, in tests/test_plan.py, tests/test_store.py, tests/test_spec_gate.py and tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n- [behavioural] the-intervention-class-type-is-the-schemas-enum.sh: a TypedDict in attavo.types for an intervention types class as the Literal of the schema's enum\ntypecheck\tmypy\t﻿2026-10-15T15:42:16.6294497Z ##[group]Run python3 -m mypy\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6294743Z ^[[36;1mpython3 -m mypy^[[0m\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6350732Z shell: /usr/bin/bash -e {0}\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6350943Z env:\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6351170Z   pythonLocation: /opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.11.17/x64\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6351515Z   PKG_CONFIG_PATH: /opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.11.17/x64/lib/pkgconfig\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6351855Z   Python_ROOT_DIR: /opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.11.17/x64\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6352157Z   Python2_ROOT_DIR: /opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.11.17/x64\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6352457Z   Python3_ROOT_DIR: /opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.11.17/x64\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6352753Z   LD_LIBRARY_PATH: /opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.11.17/x64/lib\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:16.6353010Z ##[endgroup]\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:19.3474424Z attavo/attest.py:381: error: Incompatible types (expression has type \"list[dict[str, Any]]\", TypedDict item \"interventions\" has type \"list[StatementIntervention]\")  [typeddict-item]\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:20.4126715Z Found 1 error in 1 file (checked 91 source files)\ntypecheck\tmypy\t2026-10-15T15:42:20.4246008Z ##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\n{\"type\":\"system